From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: cix: mvx: make mvx_mmu_pages.pages a flexible array member

struct mvx_mmu_pages ends with a zero-length array (phys_addr_t pages[0]).
Indexing it triggers CONFIG_UBSAN_BOUNDS reports, "array-index-out-of-bounds
in drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_mmu.c", whenever a V4L2 session
allocates, resizes or frees its pages, for example when Firefox opens a
decoder or when running an HEVC encode with hevc_v4l2m2m.

Use a C99 flexible array member instead. No functional change.

Tested on an Orange Pi 6 Plus (CIX CD8180) with 6.18.14 and the Sky1
series: a 2h44 HEVC encode with hevc_v4l2m2m (about 313 fps) no longer logs
any UBSAN report. Without the patch the same encode logs them at
mvx_mmu.c:359 (remap_pages) and :1017 (mvx_mmu_free_pages).

Signed-off-by: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_mmu.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertions(+), 1 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_mmu.h b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_mmu.h
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_mmu.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_mmu.h
@@ -126,7 +126,7 @@ struct mvx_mmu_pages {
     size_t count;
     bool is_external;
     struct list_head dmabuf;
-    phys_addr_t pages[0];
+    phys_addr_t pages[];
 };
 
 /**
